# AI-Based Accident Detection and Alert System Using ESP32

An AI-based accident detection and alert system designed to detect potential vehicle accidents and automatically send an emergency alert containing the vehicle's location.

The system combines an **ESP32**, **MPU6050 motion sensor**, **GPS**, **GSM**, **LCD**, **buzzer**, and an **AI/ML model trained using Edge Impulse** to create a real-time accident detection and notification system.

## Project Overview

Road accidents can require immediate emergency response. This project aims to detect abnormal vehicle movements associated with accidents and automatically notify a predefined contact when an accident is detected.

The system continuously monitors motion data from the MPU6050 sensor. When the AI-based detection system identifies an accident, the system starts a confirmation countdown. If the user does not cancel the alert using the push button, the system obtains the vehicle's GPS location and sends an SMS through the GSM module.

