## Accident Detection

The MPU6050 provides motion and acceleration data to the ESP32.

An AI/ML model was trained using **Edge Impulse** using collected normal-movement and accident-related data.

The trained model is used as part of the accident detection process to distinguish abnormal motion patterns from normal vehicle movement.

## Dataset

The machine learning dataset was collected using the MPU6050 sensor and includes examples of:

- Normal driving movements
- Straight forward movement
- Straight backward movement
- Gentle turns
- Start/stop movements
- Mixed normal driving
- Accident-related movement data

The dataset was prepared and uploaded to Edge Impulse for model training.

## Emergency Alert

When an accident is detected and the cancellation button is not pressed during the confirmation countdown, the system attempts to obtain the vehicle's GPS coordinates.

The system then creates a Google Maps location link and sends the location through the GSM module.

Example alert format:

```text
ACCIDENT DETECTED!

Location:
https://maps.google.com/?q=LATITUDE,LONGITUDE
```

## Hardware Communication

The project uses different communication interfaces for the connected modules:

### I2C

The ESP32 communicates with the MPU6050 and LCD through I2C.

### UART / Serial

GPS and GSM communication use serial communication with the ESP32.

### GSM

The SIM800L module is used to transmit emergency SMS messages.

